FOCUSED VALIDATION
One pass in the Preview at ~1440×900 and ~375×667. No route crawls and no repeated screenshot loops.
1. Before testing, record the seeded cases' counts (entities, events, evidence) so you can prove they are unchanged afterwards.
2. Logo: check for the valid asset. If present, inspect the landing, sign-in/register, and workspace headers for the same image, no duplicates, no crop, no distortion, and no filters. If absent, confirm the fallback renders the existing logo with no broken image.
3. Create a validation case with: a title; two linked entities; two transactions in DIFFERENT currencies; one dated event and one undated event; one evidence record. Save it, confirm it becomes active, and confirm the header, KPIs, evidence list, timeline order, graph, warnings, and report show exactly those entries, with totals grouped by currency and no fabricated zeros.
4. Switch to a seeded case and confirm it is intact and shows no leaked records. Switch back to the new case and confirm the same.
5. Edit one event or relationship and confirm the graph, timeline, KPIs, and report update. Remove one relationship and confirm exactly that edge disappears.
6. Export PDF and JSON from the new case. Check the %PDF header, page count, size, and readability where tools allow. Parse the JSON and compare its record counts with the UI. A download blocked by Preview is reported as such.
7. Reload the Preview and check whether the new case persisted. Report the real result, including a blocked-storage fallback.
8. Prism: inspect the depth and status cycle (normal and reduced-motion if emulable), checking there is no layout shift and no clipping.
9. Stepper: test 1 → 2, 1 → 5, a backward move, and a rapid second click. Confirm a ~450–550 ms pulse, an immediate target, and no intermediate activation.
10. Cleanup: delete the validation case and any stored test records, and confirm the seeded-case counts match step 1.
11. Run the existing TypeScript/build check once at the end if command execution exists; otherwise report "not run". Review the final diff, or the edit history if no diff is exposed.

